  "summary_en": "Minnesota statute regulating large warehouse distribution employers' productivity quotas: requires written quota disclosure, protects breaks, gives workers access to their work speed data, triggers investigation for high injury rates, and provides enforcement and a private right of action. Algorithmic monitoring is implicit but no AI or robots are mentioned.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must give written plain-language descriptions of quotas and notice before increases",
   "Quotas cannot prevent meal, rest, prayer or restroom breaks",
   "Employees can request 90 days of personal and aggregated work speed data",
   "Injury rates 30% above NAICS average trigger commissioner investigation and monthly safety committee meetings",
   "Enforced by the commissioner, with a private right of action within one year"
  ],
